From a6384cd2faad1b9a3dd9a264bc6ae6fe40ee5955 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hoangvu12 <hggaming91@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:21:45 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Every device registers its signing key on the account,
 headless Linux included, without signing out

A device's signing key was registered only when the desktop engine did
the sign-in itself: `zeron login` held the fresh ticket, never registered
and exited, so headless Linux never registered, and devices signed in from
before keys existed never did either. Unregistered, the Tailscale road
refuses the device, its relay dials go unstamped and its plugins unsigned.

- zeron login registers this device's key with its sign-in's ticket
  before it exits (POST /plugin-keys with stepUp); the ticket stays in
  memory only.
- Already signed in, zeron login --confirm (or zeron login on a terminal
  with the key unregistered) runs a paste-code step-up as the signed-in
  account and registers the key; the session stays as it is, another
  account's sign-in is refused, the code prompt times out.
- Desktop: Settings > Account says whether this device's key is
  registered and why not (key_status), and offers Confirm it's you: the
  existing StepUp ({for: "key"}), its ticket let go once the key
  registers with it. No sign-out.
- Registered by the edge's word, not the file's; a revoked key is
  replaced and registered again once; a key replaced by zeron login
  re-signs this device's plugins at the next engine start; a revocation
  zeron login found is answered at the next start, once, before start
  spawns anything; only a delete's step-up can delete the account.
- Failures are said: zeron login prints them and fails; the app shows
  them, and a refused step-up at once.

Tests: auth's 10 new, key_status' 4, plugins identity's 2 new,
device_key's 1, key_cli's 1, zeron-cli's login_takes_confirm, zgx
key_confirm's 3 (Rust) and 4 (Luau).
